---
title: Bolognese
servings: 6
course: Main
prep time: 15m
cook time: 1h20m
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
cuisine: Italian
---

Fry the @onions{2%large}(finely chopped) until soft but not brown. Add the @beef mince{1%kg} and cook until browned all over, breaking up any lumps.

Add the @carrots{3%large}(sliced) and @celery{3%sticks}(sliced) and cook until they soften.

Add the @mushrooms{6%medium}(sliced), @garlic{5%cloves}(crushed), @chopped tomatoes{2%tins × 400 g}, @tomato purée{1%tube}, @red wine{300%ml}, @oregano or other herbs{}, @beef stock cubes{2}, and @Worcestershire sauce{}. Bring to a boil, and then reduce to a simmer. Cook for around ~{1%hour}, stirring occasionally.

> Serve with spaghetti or other pasta.